00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:39.440
worth it. But, computers have come a long way&nbsp;
since then and anti virus software has become a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:45.200
sort of relic of computer history. To be honest,&nbsp;
I’m not complaining because while I have some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:52.000
fond memories of using Windows XP with McAfee, I&nbsp;
always hated McAfee. That crap made the computer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:58.640
slow and laggy, and I’m glad we no longer have to&nbsp;
deal with anti virus software, but how could this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:05.440
be. Every year, cyber crime is becoming a larger&nbsp;
and larger threat and the tech industry is pouring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:10.800
increasingly large amounts into fighting against&nbsp;
hackers and criminals. Well, join me as we take a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:24.495
look back how anti virus protection somehow lost&nbsp;
its place in our increasingly tech driven world.

